module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.CrystalConnection

/-!
# The canonical integrable connection on the crystalline structure sheaf

Fix a global crystalline situation `(p, (S, I, γ), X)` of [Stacks, Tag 07MF].  Over an object
`(U, T, δ)` of the big crystalline category `CRIS(X/S)` the sections of the structure sheaf
`𝒪_{X/S}` are `Γ(T, 𝒪_T)` and the sections of `Ω_{X/S}` are the divided power differentials of
that ring relative to `Γ(S, 𝒪_S)` modulo the differentials of the sections pulled back from the
base, a quotient of the Kähler differentials `Ω[Γ(T, 𝒪_T)⁄Γ(S, 𝒪_S)]`.  The quotient map is
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.crysPi`; it is surjective and its kernel is generated by
good generators, so the de Rham differential descends along it by [Stacks, Tag 07HY].

A *connection* on a module over a ring, relative to such a quotient map, is
`Crystalline.Connection` of [Stacks, Tag 07I0]: an additive map `∇ : M → M ⊗ Ω` obeying
`∇ (b · m) = b · ∇ m + m ⊗ π (d b)`, and it is *integrable*,
`Crystalline.Connection.IsIntegrable`, when its composite with its own degree-one extension
vanishes.  The structure sheaf carries the connection `∇ b = 1 ⊗ π (d b)`, built here for an
arbitrary such `π` as `Crystalline.deRhamConnection` and specialised to `𝒪_{X/S}` as
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.structureSheafConnection`; it is the universal
`S`-derivation `d_{X/S}` of [Stacks, Tag 07IX].  It is integrable because the descended de Rham
differential commutes with `π` and the de Rham complex of a ring is a complex, and its extension
to differential forms is, degree by degree, the crystalline de Rham differential of
[Stacks, Tag 07J4] — the wedge term of the extension being exactly the Leibniz term of
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.CrysDeRhamComplex.differential_smul`.

## Main definitions

* `Crystalline.deRhamConnection` — the connection `b ↦ 1 ⊗ π (d b)` on a ring, relative to a map
  out of its Kähler differentials.
* `Crystalline.dpConstPi` — the presentation of the divided power differentials killing a set of
  constants as a quotient of the Kähler differentials.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.crysPi` — that presentation for the sections of
  `Ω_{X/S}` over an object of `CRIS(X/S)`.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.structureSheafConnection` — **the canonical connection
  on `𝒪_{X/S}`**, [Stacks, Tag 07J6] for `F = 𝒪_{X/S}`.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.crysExtension` and
  `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.crysExtensionDifferential` — its extension to
  differential forms and the differential that extension carries.

## Main results

* `Crystalline.canonicalSourceDeRham_d_one_D` — the de Rham differential of a ring kills an exact
  one-form.
* `Crystalline.deRhamConnection_isIntegrable` — the connection `b ↦ 1 ⊗ π (d b)` is integrable.
* `Crystalline.extendedConnection_satisfiesRule` — the differential carried by the canonical
  extension of a connection obeys the rule of [Stacks, Tag 07HY] on the standard generators.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.surjective_crysPi` and
  `generationHypothesis_crysPi` — the two hypotheses under which the de Rham differential descends
  to `Ω^*_{X/S}` over an object.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.structureSheafConnection_apply` — the canonical
  connection on `𝒪_{X/S}` is `d_{X/S}`.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.structureSheafConnection_isIntegrable` —
  **[Stacks, Tag 07J6] for `F = 𝒪_{X/S}`**: that connection is integrable.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.crysExtensionDifferential_eq` and
  `structureSheafConnection_extension_tmul` — the extension of the canonical connection on
  `𝒪_{X/S}` is the crystalline de Rham differential of [Stacks, Tag 07J4].

## What is and is not proved

[Stacks, Tag 07J6] itself — a crystal on the small site `Cris(X/S)` has a canonical integrable
connection — is formalized, with no quasi-coherence hypothesis, in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/SmallSite/CrystalIntegrableConnectionCris.lean`,
in the namespace `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite`: the connection
`crystalConnectionCris : F ⟶ F ⊗ Ω_{X/S}`, a morphism of abelian sheaves on `Cris(X/S)`, and the
theorems `crystalConnectionCris_isConnection` and `crystalConnectionCris_isIntegrable`.  This
module is about the big site `CRIS(X/S)` and carries no attribute for that tag.

[Stacks, Tag 07J6] says that *every* crystal `F` in `𝒪_{X/S}`-modules on `Cris(X/S)` comes
equipped with a canonical integrable connection.  What is proved here is that tag for the single
crystal `F = 𝒪_{X/S}`, in the statement that the structure sheaf carries the connection
`d_{X/S}` and that this connection is integrable.  Nothing about a general crystal is proved, and
the crystal condition `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.IsCrystal` is not used.

That the connection produced here is the *canonical* one of the tag — the one read off the two
maps `p₀, p₁` of the first-order universal thickening `(U, T', δ')` of [Stacks, Tag 07J2] through
the comparison isomorphisms of the crystal — is not a theorem of this file.  For `F = 𝒪_{X/S}`
those comparison isomorphisms are the identity of `𝒪_{T'}` and the tag's recipe returns the class
of `p₁ b - p₀ b` in the ideal of `T → T'`, which
`Crystalline.firstOrderThickeningP₁_sub_P₀_eq_kernel` identifies with the universal divided power
differential `d b`; so the connection below is the canonical one.  Turning that into a Lean
theorem is blocked by one thing only.

That `(U, T', δ')` is an *object* of `CRIS(X/S)` is not in the way: the sheaf of divided power
differentials is quasi-coherent by `Crystalline.dpDifferentialsSheaf_isQuasicoherent`
[Stacks, Tag 07IY], `Stacks.Thickenings.squareZeroExtension_realization` therefore
applies, and `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.firstOrderThickeningObject` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/UniversalThickeningScheme.lean` is the object of the
site, with its three morphisms and the two diagram relations.  The tag's recipe for a *general*
sheaf of `𝒪_{X/S}`-modules is built on it, as
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.crystalConnection` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/CrystalConnectionGeneral.lean`.

What remains is the second blocker: the two spellings of `Ω` differ.  The thickening of
[Stacks, Tag 07J2] is built from the *sheaf* `Ω_{T/S,δ}`, the sheafification of the presheaf of
[Stacks, Tag 07IY], whereas the de Rham complex of [Stacks, Tag 07J4] and the connection below
live on the presheaf `Ω_{X/S}` of [Stacks, Tag 07IX];
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.restrictedToSheaf` is only a morphism between them, not
an isomorphism.  So the identity `p₁ b - p₀ b = d b` of the tag's recipe, which
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.crystalConnection_unit` proves in the sheaf spelling,
is not an identity between the connection below and that recipe.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07J6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07J6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07J4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07J4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07J2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07J2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07I0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07I0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07HY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07HY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07MF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07MF)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

noncomputable section

namespace Crystalline

open Stacks.DeRham.DifferentialDescent

/-! ### The connection on the ring itself -/

section DeRhamConnection

variable {A B Omega : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
  [AddCommGroup Omega] [Module B Omega] (pi : Ω[B⁄A] →ₗ[B] Omega)

/-- **The de Rham differential kills an exact one-form.**  This is the degree-one instance of the
complex property of the de Rham complex of `B` over `A`, read on the one-form `d b`: the latter is
the de Rham differential of `b` in degree zero. -/
theorem canonicalSourceDeRham_d_one_D (b : B) :
    (canonicalSourceDeRham A B).d 1
        ((exteriorPower.oneEquiv B (Ω[B⁄A])).symm (KaehlerDifferential.D A B b)) = 0 := by
  have hgen := KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential_smul_ιMulti_D (A := A) (B := B) 1
    (Fin.cons 1 (fun _ : Fin 1 ↦ b))
  simp only [Fin.cons_zero, Fin.cons_succ, one_smul] at hgen
  have h0 : (exteriorPower.oneEquiv B (Ω[B⁄A])).symm (KaehlerDifferential.D A B b) =
      exteriorPower.ιMulti B 1 (fun _ : Fin 1 ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B b) :=
    exteriorPower.oneEquiv_symm_apply _ _ _
  rw [h0]
  show KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential (A := A) 1 _ = 0
  rw [hgen]
  exact (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 2).map_coord_zero (i := 0) (by simp)

/-- **The canonical connection on the ring itself**, relative to a map `π` from the Kähler
differentials of `B` over `A`: the additive map `b ↦ 1 ⊗ π (d b)`, the one whose Leibniz rule
is the Leibniz rule of the universal derivation. -/
def deRhamConnection : Connection A B pi B where
  toAddMonoidHom :=
    AddMonoidHom.mk' (fun b ↦ (1 : B) ⊗ₜ[B] pi (KaehlerDifferential.D A B b))
      (fun b b' ↦ by rw [map_add, map_add, TensorProduct.tmul_add])
  leibniz' b m := by
    have key : ∀ (c : B) (x : Omega), c • ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[B] x) = c ⊗ₜ[B] x := fun c x ↦ by
      rw [TensorProduct.smul_tmul', smul_eq_mul, mul_one]
    change (1 : B) ⊗ₜ[B] pi (KaehlerDifferential.D A B (b • m)) =
      b • ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[B] pi (KaehlerDifferential.D A B m)) +
        m ⊗ₜ[B] pi (KaehlerDifferential.D A B b)
    rw [smul_eq_mul, (KaehlerDifferential.D A B).leibniz, map_add, map_smul, map_smul,
      TensorProduct.tmul_add, TensorProduct.tmul_smul, TensorProduct.tmul_smul,
      key m (pi (KaehlerDifferential.D A B b))]

/-- The value of the canonical connection on the ring itself. -/
theorem deRhamConnection_apply (b : B) :
    deRhamConnection pi b = (1 : B) ⊗ₜ[B] pi (KaehlerDifferential.D A B b) := rfl

/-- The canonical connection on the ring itself vanishes on `1`. -/
theorem deRhamConnection_one : deRhamConnection pi (1 : B) = 0 := by
  rw [deRhamConnection_apply, Derivation.map_one_eq_zero, map_zero, TensorProduct.tmul_zero]

/-- **The canonical connection on the ring itself is integrable.**  Its curvature composite is the
degree-one descended de Rham differential applied to the exact one-form `π (d b)`, which vanishes
because the descended differential commutes with `π` and the de Rham differential of `B` over `A`
is a complex. -/
theorem deRhamConnection_isIntegrable (hpi : Function.Surjective pi)
    (hgen : (canonicalSourceDeRham A B).GenerationHypothesis pi) :
    Connection.IsIntegrable (canonicalSourceDeRham A B) pi hpi hgen (deRhamConnection pi) := by
  refine Connection.isIntegrable_of_comp_eq_zero fun m ↦ ?_
  have harg : TensorProduct.map LinearMap.id
        (exteriorPower.oneEquiv B Omega).symm.toLinearMap (deRhamConnection pi m) =
      (1 : B) ⊗ₜ[B] (exteriorPower.oneEquiv B Omega).symm (pi (KaehlerDifferential.D A B m)) := by
    rw [deRhamConnection_apply, TensorProduct.map_tmul]
    rfl
  have hmap : (exteriorPower.oneEquiv B Omega).symm (pi (KaehlerDifferential.D A B m)) =
      exteriorPower.map 1 pi
        ((exteriorPower.oneEquiv B (Ω[B⁄A])).symm (KaehlerDifferential.D A B m)) := by
    rw [exteriorPower.oneEquiv_symm_apply, exteriorPower.oneEquiv_symm_apply,
      exteriorPower.map_apply_ιMulti]
    rfl
  have hz : (extendedConnection (canonicalSourceDeRham A B) pi hpi hgen
        (deRhamConnection pi)).deRhamDifferential 1
      ((exteriorPower.oneEquiv B Omega).symm (pi (KaehlerDifferential.D A B m))) = 0 := by
    rw [hmap, (extendedConnection (canonicalSourceDeRham A B) pi hpi hgen
      (deRhamConnection pi)).commutes 1, canonicalSourceDeRham_d_one_D]
    exact map_zero _
  have h := (extendedConnection (canonicalSourceDeRham A B) pi hpi hgen
    (deRhamConnection pi)).map_tmul 1 (1 : B)
      ((exteriorPower.oneEquiv B Omega).symm (pi (KaehlerDifferential.D A B m)))
  rw [deRhamConnection_one, map_zero, zero_add, hz, map_zero, TensorProduct.tmul_zero] at h
  rw [harg]
  exact (RestrictScalars.addEquiv A B _).injective (h.trans (map_zero _).symm)

/-- **The descended de Rham differential carried by the canonical extension of a connection obeys
the rule on the standard generators.**  The extension chooses the differential supplied by
[Stacks, Tag 07HY], whose commuting squares determine it, and that differential obeys the rule. -/
theorem extendedConnection_satisfiesRule {M : Type u} [AddCommGroup M] [Module B M]
    (Src : SourceDeRham A B) (hpi : Function.Surjective pi) (hgen : Src.GenerationHypothesis pi)
    (nabla : Connection A B pi M) :
    SourceDeRham.SatisfiesRule pi
      (extendedConnection Src pi hpi hgen nabla).deRhamDifferential := by
  obtain ⟨-, hr, huniq, -⟩ := Classical.choose_spec
    (exists_unique_quotient_deRhamDifferential Src pi hpi hgen)
  rw [huniq _ (extendedConnection Src pi hpi hgen nabla).commutes]
  exact hr

end DeRhamConnection

/-! ### The presentation of the divided power differentials killing a set of constants -/

section ConstPi

variable {A B : CommRingCat.{u}} {J : Ideal B}

/-- **The presentation of the divided power differentials killing a set of constants as a
quotient of the Kähler differentials**: the quotient by the divided power relations followed by
the quotient by the differentials of the constants. -/
abbrev dpConstPi (f : A ⟶ B) (hJ : DividedPowers J) (T : Set B) :
    ↥(CommRingCat.KaehlerDifferential f) →ₗ[↥B] ↥(dpConstDifferentials f hJ T) :=
  (dpMkQ f hJ ≫ dpConstMk f hJ T).hom

/-- The presentation carries the universal derivation of the Kähler differentials to the universal
divided power differential killing the constants. -/
theorem dpConstPi_d (f : A ⟶ B) (hJ : DividedPowers J) (T : Set B) (b : B) :
    dpConstPi f hJ T (CommRingCat.KaehlerDifferential.d b) = (dpConstD f hJ T).d b := rfl

/-- The presentation is surjective, being a composite of two quotient maps. -/
theorem surjective_dpConstPi (f : A ⟶ B) (hJ : DividedPowers J) (T : Set B) :
    Function.Surjective (dpConstPi f hJ T) := by
  intro y
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mkQ_surjective (dpBaseRelations f hJ T) y
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mkQ_surjective (dpRelations f hJ) x
  exact ⟨z, rfl⟩

/-- **The presentation satisfies the generation hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 07HY]**, its kernel
being the join of the divided power relations with the span of the differentials of the
constants. -/
theorem generationHypothesis_dpConstPi (f : A ⟶ B) (hJ : DividedPowers J) (T : Set B) :
    letI := f.hom.toAlgebra
    (canonicalSourceDeRham ↥A ↥B).GenerationHypothesis (dpConstPi f hJ T) := by
  let _ := f.hom.toAlgebra
  exact generationHypothesis_of_ker_eq_sup hJ T (dpConstPi f hJ T)
    (ker_mkQ_comp_mkQ_image _ (KaehlerDifferential.D ↥A ↥B) T)

end ConstPi

/-! ### The structure sheaf of the crystalline site -/

namespace GlobalCrystallineSituation

variable (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u})

/-- **The presentation of the sections of `Ω_{X/S}` over an object of `CRIS(X/S)` as a quotient of
the Kähler differentials** of the sections of `𝒪_T` over the global sections of the divided power
base. -/
abbrev crysPi (A : Thickening S) :
    Ω[crysFormRing S A⁄↥Γ(S.S.scheme, ⊤)] →ₗ[crysFormRing S A]
      ↥((crysDifferentials S).obj (op A)) :=
  dpConstPi (crysBaseAppLE S A) (crysDividedPowers S A) (crysBaseSections S A)

/-- The presentation carries the universal derivation of the Kähler differentials to the universal
divided power derivation `d_{X/S}`. -/
theorem crysPi_D (A : Thickening S) (b : crysFormRing S A) :
    crysPi S A (KaehlerDifferential.D ↥Γ(S.S.scheme, ⊤) (crysFormRing S A) b) =
      crysD S A b := rfl

/-- The presentation of the sections of `Ω_{X/S}` over an object is surjective. -/
theorem surjective_crysPi (A : Thickening S) : Function.Surjective (crysPi S A) :=
  surjective_dpConstPi (crysBaseAppLE S A) (crysDividedPowers S A) (crysBaseSections S A)

/-- The presentation of the sections of `Ω_{X/S}` over an object satisfies the generation
hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 07HY]. -/
theorem generationHypothesis_crysPi (A : Thickening S) :
    (canonicalSourceDeRham ↥Γ(S.S.scheme, ⊤) (crysFormRing S A)).GenerationHypothesis
      (crysPi S A) :=
  generationHypothesis_dpConstPi (crysBaseAppLE S A) (crysDividedPowers S A)
    (crysBaseSections S A)

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07J6, for `F = 𝒪_{X/S}`.**  The canonical connection that the structure
sheaf of the crystalline site carries over an object `(U, T, δ)` of `CRIS(X/S)`: the universal
`S`-derivation `d_{X/S}`, as a connection on `Γ(T, 𝒪_T)` relative to the presentation of the
sections of `Ω_{X/S}` there.  It is the connection of the tag for the crystal `𝒪_{X/S}`, whose
comparison isomorphisms are the identity, so that the tag's recipe through the first-order
universal thickening of [Stacks, Tag 07J2] returns `p₁ - p₀ = d_{X/S}`; see the implementation
notes for why that identification is not itself a theorem here. -/
def structureSheafConnection (A : Thickening S) :
    Connection ↥Γ(S.S.scheme, ⊤) (crysFormRing S A) (crysPi S A) (crysFormRing S A) :=
  deRhamConnection (crysPi S A)

/-- The canonical connection on `𝒪_{X/S}` is the universal `S`-derivation `d_{X/S}`. -/
theorem structureSheafConnection_apply (A : Thickening S) (b : crysFormRing S A) :
    structureSheafConnection S A b =
      (1 : crysFormRing S A) ⊗ₜ[crysFormRing S A] crysD S A b := rfl

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07J6, for `F = 𝒪_{X/S}`.**  The canonical connection on the structure
sheaf is integrable: its curvature composite is the degree-one de Rham differential of the exact
one-form `d_{X/S} b`, which vanishes. -/
theorem structureSheafConnection_isIntegrable (A : Thickening S) :
    Connection.IsIntegrable (canonicalSourceDeRham ↥Γ(S.S.scheme, ⊤) (crysFormRing S A))
      (crysPi S A) (surjective_crysPi S A) (generationHypothesis_crysPi S A)
      (structureSheafConnection S A) :=
  deRhamConnection_isIntegrable (crysPi S A) (surjective_crysPi S A)
    (generationHypothesis_crysPi S A)

/-- The extension to differential forms of the canonical connection on `𝒪_{X/S}`. -/
def crysExtension (A : Thickening S) :
    ExtendedConnection (canonicalSourceDeRham ↥Γ(S.S.scheme, ⊤) (crysFormRing S A))
      (crysPi S A) (structureSheafConnection S A) :=
  extendedConnection (canonicalSourceDeRham ↥Γ(S.S.scheme, ⊤) (crysFormRing S A))
    (crysPi S A) (surjective_crysPi S A) (generationHypothesis_crysPi S A)
    (structureSheafConnection S A)

/-- The degree-`i` differential that the extension of the canonical connection on `𝒪_{X/S}`
carries, retyped as a homomorphism of additive groups on the exterior powers of `Ω_{X/S}`. -/
def crysExtensionDifferential (A : Thickening S) (i : ℕ) :
    ⋀[crysFormRing S A]^i ((crysDifferentials S).obj (op A)) →+
      ⋀[crysFormRing S A]^(i + 1) ((crysDifferentials S).obj (op A)) :=
  AddMonoidHom.mk' (fun ω ↦ (crysExtension S A).deRhamDifferential i ω)
    (fun x y ↦ map_add _ x y)

/-- **The differential carried by the extension of the canonical connection on `𝒪_{X/S}` is the
crystalline de Rham differential of [Stacks, Tag 07J4].**  Both are additive and linear over the
global sections of the divided power base and obey the same rule on the standard generators, which
determines them. -/
theorem crysExtensionDifferential_eq (A : Thickening S) (i : ℕ) :
    crysExtensionDifferential S A i = (crysDeRhamComplex S).differential i A := by
  refine dpConstDeRham_unique (crysBaseAppLE S A) (crysDividedPowers S A)
    (crysBaseSections S A) i (fun a ω ↦ ?_) (fun a ω ↦ ?_) (fun b ↦ ?_) (fun b ↦ ?_)
  · exact (crysExtension S A).deRhamDifferential i |>.map_smul a ω
  · exact (crysDeRhamComplex S).differential_base_smul i A a ω
  · exact extendedConnection_satisfiesRule (crysPi S A)
      (canonicalSourceDeRham ↥Γ(S.S.scheme, ⊤) (crysFormRing S A)) (surjective_crysPi S A)
      (generationHypothesis_crysPi S A) (structureSheafConnection S A) i b
  · exact (crysDeRhamComplex S).differential_generator i A b

/-- **The extension to differential forms of the canonical connection on `𝒪_{X/S}` is the
crystalline de Rham differential of [Stacks, Tag 07J4].**  Under the identification
`𝒪_{X/S} ⊗ Ω^i_{X/S} = Ω^i_{X/S}` the degree-`i` extension sends `m ⊗ ω` to `d (m · ω)`: the
wedge term of the extension is the Leibniz term of
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.CrysDeRhamComplex.differential_smul`. -/
theorem structureSheafConnection_extension_tmul (A : Thickening S) (i : ℕ)
    (m : crysFormRing S A)
    (ω : ⋀[crysFormRing S A]^i ((crysDifferentials S).obj (op A))) :
    RestrictScalars.addEquiv ↥Γ(S.S.scheme, ⊤) (crysFormRing S A)
        ((crysFormRing S A) ⊗[crysFormRing S A]
          ⋀[crysFormRing S A]^(i + 1) ((crysDifferentials S).obj (op A)))
        ((crysExtension S A).toLinearMap i (m ⊗ₜ[crysFormRing S A] ω)) =
      (1 : crysFormRing S A) ⊗ₜ[crysFormRing S A]
        (crysDeRhamComplex S).differential i A (m • ω) := by
  have key : ∀ (c : crysFormRing S A)
      (x : ⋀[crysFormRing S A]^(i + 1) ((crysDifferentials S).obj (op A))),
      c ⊗ₜ[crysFormRing S A] x = (1 : crysFormRing S A) ⊗ₜ[crysFormRing S A] (c • x) := by
    intro c x
    rw [TensorProduct.tmul_smul, TensorProduct.smul_tmul', smul_eq_mul, mul_one]
  have hd : RestrictScalars.addEquiv ↥Γ(S.S.scheme, ⊤) (crysFormRing S A) _
      ((crysExtension S A).deRhamDifferential i ω) =
      (crysDeRhamComplex S).differential i A ω :=
    congrArg (fun g ↦ g ω) (crysExtensionDifferential_eq S A i)
  rw [(crysExtension S A).map_tmul i m ω, structureSheafConnection_apply,
    TensorProduct.map_tmul, LinearMap.id_apply, LinearMap.flip_apply, hd,
    key m ((crysDeRhamComplex S).differential i A ω),
    CrysDeRhamComplex.differential_smul S (crysDeRhamComplex S) i A m ω,
    ← TensorProduct.tmul_add]
  exact congrArg _ (add_comm _ _)

end GlobalCrystallineSituation

end Crystalline

end

end
